# bron-resins catalog -- working-tier SHA3-256 names when sealed; plain paths today
#
# THE PROMISE THIS FILE KEEPS. `foundations/20260703-202312_the-marked-value.md` states the
# cellar's own clause: *every resin records the marks of what it seals, so a reader in another
# decade knows what the cellar held without opening it.* One `entry` line per resin is how that
# promise is kept at plain-path tier, and the `note` below is the habit that keeps it current.
#
# REFRESHED `20260906.233111`, after a measurement. The habit was kept for the first three files
# of the first morning and dropped: the room held 17 resins and this catalog named 3, and nothing
# in the tree read it -- three scans name `bron-resins/` only to skip it as testimony. A catalog
# covering a fifth of its room reads exactly like a whole one. Fourteen entries were written from
# each resin's OWN first header line rather than from a summary, and the catalog now has a reader:
# `tools/b/bron_resins_catalog_witness.rish` holds uncatalogued, orphaned, and duplicated lines at
# zero on every lap, so this file can never quietly go stale again.
format bron-resins-v1
stamp 20260712.115753
refreshed 20260906.233111
purpose chat-printout essay resins as Bron values at the seam
law Bron carries immutable values; Brix composes wholes; this folder holds Bron only
witness tools/b/bron_resins_catalog_witness.rish -- uncatalogued, orphan, and duplicate lines at zero
entry 20260712-115753_morning-fold-thoughts.bron fuller morning summary and Rio essay as chat-printout-v1
